=head1 NAME

RECALIBRATE_TSYS - Calculate and apply new TSYS correction factor

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This recipe attempts to recalibrate data by adjusting the TSYS correction
factor.  This is only relevant to receivers using the 2-load calibration
scheme (i.e. Namakanui).

=head1 RECIPE PARAMETERS

=over 2

=item CAL_AM

Airmass to use for calculations.  Can be "ref" (computed airmass
for position of reference at the time) or "tcs" (TCS airmass
value in JCMTSTATE).  [ref]

=item CAL_DATA

How to select data to use in the calibration recalculation.  Can be
"start" (start of the observation), "cal" (step after the last
calibration) or "step" (the step at which a change in Tsys was
identified).  [cal]

=item ETA_TEL

How to determine the ETA_TEL (telescope efficiency) parameter to use.
Can be "header" (FITS header), "tabulated" (value tabulated in this
recipe), "auto" (to use the header value unless it deviates too far
from the tabulated value) or a specific decimal value.  (Abbreviations
of some of these options can also be used.)  [auto]

=item ETA_TEL_TOL

If C<ETA_TEL> is "auto", the tolerance from the tabulated value.  [0.05]

=item VERBOSE

Whether to include more verbose output.  [0]

=back

